{"uid":"6ce46d07faf52516","name":"test_verified_review_refused_while_steering_pending","fullName":"tests.test_e2e#test_verified_review_refused_while_steering_pending","historyId":"7f31e5b13c4791baf328b7fcf2909b9f","time":{"start":1791891379222,"stop":1791891380507,"duration":1285},"description":"Task 005 regression: steering that lands during the review iteration of\n    what would otherwise be the final VERIFIED verdict must not be silently\n    stranded by a terminal-succeeded run. The engine must discard that verdict,\n    route back so the steering is actually settled, then re-review -- only\n    succeeding once no steering is left pending.\n\n    Task 013 (requirement I, #98) strengthens WHAT settles it. The old claim\n    was `phases == [planning, worker, review, worker, review]` with the file\n    consumed by iteration 4 -- a no-task `worker` iteration `_step_review`\n    dispatched by hand from inside its own in-place discard loop. That loop is\n    replaced by ONE deferral through the declared\n    `steering_pending_at_verified` edge, so the ordinary dispatch loop routes\n    the message to the hat that exists for it: `planning, worker, review,\n    steer, worker, review`, with `001-lastcall.md` consumed by the `steer`\n    iteration. The guarantee this test exists for is unchanged -- the run\n    still may not go terminal-succeeded with the file unconsumed -- and the\n    consumer is now a hat whose whole prompt is about operator messages\n    instead of a worker iteration with no task in hand.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 005 regression: steering that lands during the review iteration of<br />\nwhat would otherwise be the final VERIFIED verdict must not be silently<br />\nstranded by a terminal-succeeded run. The engine must discard that verdict,<br />\nroute back so the steering is actually settled, then re-review -- only<br />\nsucceeding once no steering is left pending.</p>\n<pre><code>Task 013 (requirement I, #98) strengthens WHAT settles it. The old claim\nwas `phases == [planning, worker, review, worker, review]` with the file\nconsumed by iteration 4 -- a no-task `worker` iteration `_step_review`\ndispatched by hand from inside its own in-place discard loop. That loop is\nreplaced by ONE deferral through the declared\n`steering_pending_at_verified` edge, so the ordinary dispatch loop routes\nthe message to the hat that exists for it: `planning, worker, review,\nsteer, worker, review`, with `001-lastcall.md` consumed by the `steer`\niteration. The guarantee this test exists for is unchanged -- the run\nstill may not go terminal-succeeded with the file unconsumed -- and the\nconsumer is now a hat whose whole prompt is about operator messages\ninstead of a worker iteration with no task in hand.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791891119391,"stop":1791891119391,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791891119392,"stop":1791891119392,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791891379205,"stop":1791891379205,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791891379205,"stop":1791891379211,"duration":6},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolat